ned backend binaries `/usr/local/bin/yalla-api` and\n     6\t`/usr/local/bin/yal
la-worker`, the support-only `POST /v1/admin/dokploy/import`\n     7\tendpoint, 
the Import dry-run preview gate, durable import jobs, audit evidence,\n     8\ta
nd the Yalla API -> Postgres source of truth -> provisioning worker -> private\n
    9\tDokploy API boundary. In short:\n    10\tYalla API -> Postgres source of 
truth -> provisioning worker -> private Dokploy API.\n    11\t\n    12\tCustomer
s must never receive Dokploy API tokens or call Dokploy directly. A\n    13\tten
ant import materializes controlled Yalla source-of-truth rows and\n    14\ttenan
t-scoped `dokploy_refs`; it is not a generic customer-facing proxy to\n    15\tD
okploy. The mutating endpoint is authorized through `support.manage` in the\n   
