ontract that (a) the API binary does not terminate TLS itself and\n   467\t(b) t
he rate limiter trusts only a closed set of forwarded-IP\n   468\theaders. Three
real-file matchers run alongside one synthetic\n   469\tself-check (`TestHTTPSer
verHardeningStaticAnalyzerDetectsRegressions`):\n   470\t\n   471\t- **`cmd/yall
a-api/main.go`** — `findAPITLSRegressions` walks the\n   472\t  AST and rejects:
(1) any call whose selector name is in\n   473\t  `forbiddenAPITLSCallSelectors`
(`ListenAndServeTLS`, `ServeTLS`),\n   474\t  regardless of receiver; (2) any `h
ttp.Server` composite literal\n   475\t  that omits a field from `requiredHTTPSe
rverFields`\n   476\t  (`ReadHeaderTimeout` is the Slowloris guard) OR contains 
a field\n   477\t  from `forbiddenAPITLSStructFields` (`TLSConfig`, `TLSNextProt
o`);\n   478\t  (3) any assignment whose LHS selector is in\n   479\t  `forbidde
nAPITLSStructFields` (the post-construction mutation\n   480\t  seam). The match
er uses the package-qualified type selector\n   481\t  `http.Server`, so unrelat
ed structs in `main.go` are not scanned.\n   482\t- **`internal/controlplane/htt
papi/ratelimit.go`** —\n   483\t  `findProxyHeaderTrustRegressions` runs two pas
ses. The scoped\n   484\t  pass locates the `ClientIP` function by name and walk
s every\n   485\t  `*.Header.Get("...")` inside it; any literal not in\n   486\t
 `allowedProxyHeaderLiterals` (`X-Forwarded-For`, `X-Real-IP`,\n   487\t  case-s
ensitive) is flagged. The scoped pass also asserts the\n   488\t  body reference
s `RemoteAddr` so the fallback chain stays intact.\n   489\t  The file-wide pass
walks every string literal in the file and\n   490\t  flags any whose lower-case
d form is in\n   491\t  `forbiddenProxyHeaderLiterals` (RFC 7239 `Forwarded`,\n 
 492\t  `True-Client-IP`, `CF-Connecting-IP`, `Fastly-Client-IP`,\n   493\t  `X-
Client-IP`, `X-Forwarded-{Host,Proto,Server,Port}`,\n   494\t  `X-Original-Forwa
rded-For`). If `ClientIP` is missing entirely\n   495\t  the matcher emits a sin
gle "missing function" hit so the gate\n   496\t  cannot pass silently when its 
target is removed.\n   497\t- **`SECURITY.md`** —\n   498\t  `TestHTTPServerHard
eningSecurityDocumentsTLSAndProxyTrust` pins\n   499\t  the `## TLS Termination 
and Proxy Header Trust` heading, the\n   500\t  verification-gates table row, an
d the canonical substrings\n   501\t  (`TLS is terminated at the operator\'s rev
erse proxy`,\n   502\t  `ReadHeaderTimeout`, `X-Forwarded-For`, `X-Real-IP`, and
the\n   503\t  test file path itself). The substrings carry the load-bearing\n  
504\t  facts so a future reader does not have to open the test file to\n   505\t
 learn the contract.\n   506\t\n   507\tWhen adding or removing a trusted forwar
ding header, update\n   508\t`allowedProxyHeaderLiterals` AND the `ClientIP` bod
y AND the\n   509\tSECURITY.md section in the same edit. When adding or removing
