  155\tautomatically.\n   156\t\n   157\t## Container Image Hardening\n   158\t\
n   159\tThe production `Dockerfile` ships the `yalla-api` binary and\n   160\t`
Dockerfile.worker` ships the `yalla-worker` binary inside a\n   161\t`gcr.io/dis
troless/static-debian12:nonroot` runtime so a leaked or\n   162\tcompromised ima
ge carries no shell, no package manager, no busybox,\n   163\tand no setuid bina
ries — only the service binary and the system CA\n   164\tbundle. The hardening 
posture is part of the public contract and is\n   165\tpinned by `internal/relea
se/container_hardening_static_test.go`; a\n   166\tregression in any one of the 
following is caught at build time:\n   167\t\n   168\t- **Multi-stage build.** T
he Go toolchain, module cache, and source\n   169\t  tree never reach the runtim
e layer. A single-stage Dockerfile is\n   170\t  rejected.\n   171\t- **Distrole
ss `nonroot` runtime.** The runtime stage\'s base image\n   172\t  is pinned to 
`gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot` (UID/GID\n   173\t  65532). Debian/U
buntu/Alpine slim runtimes are rejected because\n   174\t  they reintroduce a sh
ell and a package manager.\n   175\t- **`USER nonroot:nonroot`.** The runtime st
age MUST run as the\n   176\t  non-root user. A missing or partial (`USER nonroo
t`) directive is\n   177\t  rejected.\n   178\t- **Hardened build flags.** The b
uilder stage MUST invoke\n   179\t  `go build` with `CGO_ENABLED=0` (static bina
ry compatible with\n   180\t  the distroless static image), `-trimpath` (strip l
ocal filesystem\n   181\t  paths from the binary), and `-ldflags="-s -w"` (drop 
