ernal/release/... -run TestRollbackChecklistArtifact`.\n   823\t\n   824\t## TLS
Termination and Proxy Header Trust\n   825\t\n   826\tThe Yalla control-plane AP
I binary (`cmd/yalla-api`) deliberately\n   827\tdoes NOT terminate TLS itself.\
n   828\t**TLS is terminated at the operator\'s reverse proxy**\n   829\t(ingres
s controller, load balancer, or front-door proxy), which\n   830\tforwards the r
equest to the API over an internal network. Keeping certificate material out of 
the API process\n   831\tnarrows the secret surface, leverages the proxy\'s vett
ed cipher\n   832\tsuite / HSTS / OCSP stapling defaults, and lets operators rot
ate\n   833\tcertificates without an API restart. The posture is pinned by\n   8
34\t`internal/release/http_server_hardening_static_test.go`; a regression\n   83
5\tin any one of the following is caught at build time:\n   836\t\n   837\t- **N
o in-process TLS.** The API binary MUST NOT call\n   838\t  `ListenAndServeTLS` 
or `ServeTLS`, and the constructed\n   839\t  `*http.Server` MUST NOT set `TLSCo
nfig` or `TLSNextProto`. Any\n   840\t  TLS-termination shape inside the binary 
is rejected.\n   841\t- **Slowloris guard.** Every `*http.Server` literal in the
API\n   842\t  binary MUST set a positive `ReadHeaderTimeout`. The current value
\n   843\t  is `10 * time.Second`. Removing the field, or initialising the\n   8
44\t  server with the zero value, is rejected.\n   845\t- **Closed-set proxy hea
der trust.** The rate limiter resolves the\n   846\t  caller\'s identity through
`ClientIP(r)` in\n   847\t  `internal/controlplane/httpapi/ratelimit.go`. The he
lper consults\n   848\t  only two forwarding headers:\n   849\t  - `X-Forwarded-
For` — the **first hop only** is taken so a forged\n   850\t    tail entry canno
t displace the real client.\n   851\t  - `X-Real-IP` as a fallback.\n   852\t  N
o other forwarded-* family header is honoured. RFC 7239\n   853\t  `Forwarded`, 
Akamai `True-Client-IP`, Cloudflare\n   854\t  `CF-Connecting-IP`, Fastly `Fastl
y-Client-IP`, `X-Client-IP`,\n   855\t  `X-Original-Forwarded-For`, and the meta
-data variants\n   856\t  (`X-Forwarded-Host`, `X-Forwarded-Proto`, `X-Forwarded
-Port`,\n   857\t  `X-Forwarded-Server`) are deliberately ignored. If the API is
\n   858\t  ever reachable directly — a network misconfiguration, an internal\n 
 859\t  pivot, or a forgotten test fixture — an attacker who can reach it\n   86
0\t  must not be able to spoof their identity past the IP bucket by\n   861\t  s
ending one of those headers. The closed set is enforced by the\n   862\t  static
analyser; adding a new header to the trust list requires\n   863\t  an explicit,
reviewed change to the allow-list.\n   864\t\n   865\t### Operator expectations\
n   866\t\n   867\tThe reverse proxy MUST be configured to:\n   868\t\n   869\t1
. **Strip inbound `X-Forwarded-*` and `X-Real-IP` headers** from\n   870\t   pub
lic traffic before setting its own. Otherwise an attacker\n   871\t   can pre-po
pulate the header and the proxy will forward it\n   872\t   verbatim — the API w
ill then trust the attacker-supplied value.\n   873\t2. **Set `X-Forwarded-For`*
* to the immediate downstream client\'s\n   874\t   IP address. The API only rea
ds the first hop, so the proxy\'s\n   875\t   append-on-each-hop semantics are h
onoured.\n   876\t3. **Terminate TLS** with a modern cipher suite, an up-to-date
\n   877\t   certificate, and HSTS where appropriate. The API never sees\n   878
\t   the original ClientHello.\n   879\t4. **Use an internal network or loopback
** to reach the API. The\n   880\t   API listener is HTTP-only and MUST NOT be e
xposed to the\n   881\t   public internet directly.\n   882\t\n   883\t## Admin 
Endpoint Isolation\n   884\t\n   885\tThe Yalla control-plane API binary (`cmd/y
alla-api`) deliberately\n   886\tships **no `/debug/` surface**. There is no `/d
ebug/pprof/*`, no\n   887\t`/debug/vars`, no `/debug/requests`, and no `/debug/e
vents` route on\n   888\tthe customer-facing listener — neither authenticated no
r\n   889\tunauthenticated. Goroutine profiles, heap snapshots, command-line\n  
890\targuments, registered `expvar` variables, and live CPU profiles are\n   891
\tload-bearing operator-only secrets; exposing any of them on a\n   892\tlistene
r customers can reach is a build-blocking regression. The\n   893\tposture is pi
nned by\n   894\t`internal/release/admin_endpoint_isolation_static_test.go`; the
\n   895\tgate rejects any of the following shapes at build time:\n   896\t\n   
897\t- **No side-effecting debug imports.** Neither `cmd/yalla-api` nor\n   898\
t  any production source file under `internal/controlplane/httpapi`\n   899\t  m
ay import `net/http/pprof`, `expvar`, or\n   900\t  `golang.org/x/net/trace`. A 
blank import alone is sufficient to\n   901\t  register the surface on `http.Def
aultServeMux`; the matcher\n   902\t  rejects every form of import (blank, named
, aliased) of those\n   903\t  three paths.\n   904\t- **Private mux only.** `ht
tpapi.NewHandler` MUST construct its own\n   905\t  mux via `http.NewServeMux()`
and MUST NOT reference\n   906\t  `http.DefaultServeMux` anywhere. The private m
ux severs the API\n   907\t  listener from any default-mux registrations made el
sewhere in the\n   908\t  binary (a transitive dependency, a hand-rolled experim
ent, a\n   909\t  future contributor\'s debugging helper). The matcher flags the
\n   910\t  absence of `http.NewServeMux()` and any reference to\n   911\t  `Def
aultServeMux` in the handler file.\n   912\t- **Explicit `http.Server.Handler`.*
* The API binary\'s\n   913\t  `*http.Server` composite literal in `cmd/yalla-ap
i/main.go` MUST\n   914\t  set `Handler` to a non-nil value. A nil `Handler` fal
ls back to\n   915\t  `http.DefaultServeMux` per the standard library\'s documen
ted\n   916\t  contract, and that fallback would re-introduce the exposure the\n
  917\t  private-mux contract disclaims. The matcher flags both the\n   918\t  m
issing field and an explicit `Handler: nil`.\n   919\t- **No `/debug/*` literal 
or `pprof.*` / `expvar.*` selector.** No\n   920\t  production source file under
`cmd/yalla-api` or\n   921\t  `internal/controlplane/httpapi` may carry a `/debu
g/pprof`,\n   922\t  `/debug/vars`, `/debug/requests`, or `/debug/events` string
\n   923\t  literal, name `http.DefaultServeMux`, or reference a `pprof.*` or\n 
 924\t  `expvar.*` selector. The file-wide pass is belt-and-braces for\n   925\t
 the import scan: a regression that registers the routes through\n   926\t  a ha
